expected_issues.description:
Potential alignment issue: allocate() returns raw memory from JemallocNodumpAllocatorImpl without verifying it satisfies alignof(T). If the underlying allocator doesn't guarantee at least max_align_t or alignof(T), this can cause UB for over-aligned types. Consider either restricting T to not be over-aligned (static_assert) or adding an aligned allocation path.

```suggestion
        static_assert(alignof(T) <= alignof(std::max_align_t), "Over-aligned types require aligned allocation");
        void * ptr = JemallocNodumpAllocatorImpl::instance().allocate(bytes);
        if (!ptr)
            throw std::bad_alloc();
        return static_cast<T *>(ptr);
```

