expected_issues.description:
Using `boost::algorithm::unhex` directly returns a `std::string`, which creates a temporary copy of the decoded key in the default allocator (dumpable memory). This undermines the purpose of using `NoDumpString`. 

Consider decoding directly into the `key` variable using an output iterator to ensure the sensitive data remains in non-dumpable memory:

```cpp
key.reserve(key_hex.size() / 2);
boost::algorithm::unhex(key_hex, std::back_inserter(key));
```

