known_false_positives.description:
`madvise()` returns 0 on success and -1 on failure (with `errno` set). Here `ret` will be -1, but you pass `ret` into `errnoToString(ret)`, which likely prints "Unknown error -1". Capture `errno` after failure (or use `errnoToString(errno)`), and consider including address/size in the message for easier debugging.

```suggestion
        if (madvise(result, size, MADV_DONTDUMP) != 0)
        {
            const int err = errno;
            throw std::runtime_error(Poco::format("Failed to run madvise(MADV_DONTDUMP) on %p (size %zu): %s", result, size, errnoToString(err)));
        }
```
